SUMMARY:Kicking It at Hermann Park
DESCRIPTION:This summer\, Hermann Park Conservancy will welcome the world to Houston with Kicking It at Hermann Park\, presented by ExxonMobil—a free\, public celebration of culture\, community\, and the unifying spirit of sport. Featuring a dynamic mix of programming\, diverse food offerings\, live entertainment\, and family-friendly activities\, everything will take place in the Commons\, the vibrant 26-acre play and gathering space in the southwest corner of the Park. \n\n📍 The Commons at Hermann Park\n📅 Weekend and select weekdays from June 12 – July 12\n🎟️ Free & open to the public\n\nKicking It at Hermann Park will run on weekends and select weekdays from Friday\, June 12\, through Sunday\, July 12\, offering 18 days of engaging experiences for Houstonians and visitors alike during a globally significant moment for the city. \nThe roster of dynamic programming will include: \n\n🎶 Live music & entertainment\n🍴 Local food trucks & culinary offerings\n🎬 Outdoor movie nights\n⚽ Soccer-inspired play & interactive experiences\n🌿 Nature-based activities\n👨‍👩‍👧 Family-friendly programming\n🎭 Cultural celebrations highlighting Houston’s diversity\n\nThank you to ExxonMobil for their generous support! \n \n+++ \nKNOW BEFORE YOU GO! \n\nPlease note that all events are weather dependent. If storms are in the forecast\, be sure to check our website and social media for the latest updates before attending.\nStay hydrated! Bring a refillable water and fill up at water stations throughout the Park. Water and other beverages are also available for purchase at the cafes and food vendors in the Park.\nBring sunscreen and bug spray\, and be sure to reapply often if you are spending the day in the Park.\nSeating for movie night is on the grass lawn in the Commons\, so be sure to bring a blanket or lawn chair.\nVisitors can park in any of the open\, available lots within Hermann Park. The lots closest to the Commons are Lot A\, by the Japanese Garden\, and Lots E\, F\, G\, and H\, by the Houston Zoo. Lot T\, the small lot near Wortham Pavilion\, will be closed to the public and reserved for event security and medical personnel.\n\nA map of parking lots available throughout the Park can be found HERE.\n\n\nVisitors can also park at the Memorial Hermann Medical Plaza Garage (Winpark)\, located at 6400 Fannin Street\, which is across the street from the Commons site. There is a daily fee to park in this garage on the weekend.\nAdditionally\, we encourage visitors to use the METRORail Red Line’s “Hermann Park/Rice U” stop which located adjacent to a walking trail that leads directly to the Commons.\n\n+++ \nDATES & THEMES\nStay tuned for more details and a complete programming calendar. Activities are subject to change and more may be added. Visit the Conservancy tent on-site in the Commons for any questions!\n \nWEEKEND ONE (JUNE 12 – JUNE 14) PDF SCHEDULE HERE. \nWEEKEND TWO (JUNE 19 – JUNE 21) PDF SCHEDULE HERE. \nWEEKEND THREE (JUNE 26 – JUNE 29) PDF SCHEDULE HERE. \nWEEKEND FOUR (JULY 3 – JULY 5) PDF SCHEDULE HERE. \nWEEKEND FIVE (JULY 10 – JULY 12) PDF SCHEDULE HERE. \nFriday\, June 12 (5 – 9 p.m.): Kickoff in the Park \nSaturday\, June 13 (3 – 10 p.m.): Texas Heritage \nSunday\, June 14 (3 – 9 p.m.): Family & Global Community Day \nWednesday\, June 17 (3 – 9 p.m.): Wellness in the Park – THIS DATE HAS BEEN CANCELED DUE TO INCLEMENT WEATHER! \nFriday\, June 19 (5 – 9 p.m.): Juneteenth Celebration \nSaturday\, June 20 (3 – 10 p.m.): Global Rhythms \nSunday\, June 21 (3 – 9 p.m.): Community & Wellness Day \nTuesday\, June 23 (3 – 9 p.m.): Youth + Play + Sustainability Day \nFriday\, June 26 (5 – 9 p.m.): Latin Night \nSaturday\, June 27 (3 – 10 p.m.): Global DJ Night \nSunday\, June 28 (3 – 9 p.m.): International Culture Day \nMonday\, June 29 (3 – 9 p.m.): Arts + Nature Day \nFriday\, July 3 (5 – 10 p.m.): Summer Nights in the Park \nSaturday\, July 4 (3 – 11 p.m.): Celebrate America – Houston Style \nSunday\, July 5 (3 – 9 p.m.): Party in the Park \nFriday\, July 10: 713 Weekend \n\n10 AM – 12 PM: Activities with Collab-Lab by Collaborative for Children (Lake Plaza by Kinder Station and the Houston Zoo Entrance)\n5 – 7 PM: Carousel Karaoke (Lott Family Carousel in the Commons)\n6 – 8 PM: “Kick Into Creativity” Eco Art Studio (Astros Foundation Pavilion in the Commons)\n6 – 8 PM: “Soccer for Success” Open Play by Houston Parks and Recreation Department (Next to the Carousel and Play Areas in the Commons)\n7 – 8 PM: Sunset Bird Walk with Houston Audubon (Meet at Pedal Boat Kiosk in Lake Plaza) (REGISTER HERE)\n7 – 9 PM: Open Decks: Live DJ Experience with DJ Hiram (Lott Family Carousel in the Commons)\n\nSaturday\, July 11: 713 Weekend \n\n8 – 9 AM: Prioritizing Peace: Sound Bath (Tsuru Family Terrace in the Commons)\n9 AM – 12 PM: “Ask a Master Gardener” Q&A Series (Family Garden in the McGovern Centennial Gardens)\n9:30 – 10:30 AM: Zumba with Tiny Fitness (Tsuru Family Terrace in the Commons)\n5 – 8 PM: Goya Giveaways (Next to the Carousel and Play Areas in the Commons)\n6 – 8 PM: “Kick Into Creativity” Eco Art Studio (Astros Foundation Pavilion in the Commons)\n6 – 8 PM: “Soccer for Success” Open Play by Houston Parks and Recreation Department (Next to the Carousel and Play Areas in the Commons)\n6 – 8 PM: Music by DJ Hiram (Lott Family Carousel in the Commons)\n8:30 PM: “Moonlight Movie Nights” presented by Goya: A Bug’s Life (Doreen Stoller Lawn in the Commons)\n\nSunday\, July 12: 713 Weekend \n\n6 – 8 PM: Print Making by Eternal Gandhi Museum (Astros Foundation Pavilion in the Commons)\n6 – 8 PM: “Soccer for Success” Open Play by Houston Parks and Recreation Department (Next to the Carousel and Play Areas in the Commons)\n7 – 9 PM: Music by Bayou City Jazz Band (Lott Family Carousel in the Commons)\n\n+++ \nMOONLIGHT MOVIE NIGHTS\nPresented by Goya \n \nAs part of the summer offerings\, enjoy Moonlight Movie Nights\, presented by Goya\, in the Commons! Movies will start at approximately 8:30 p.m.\, around sunset. These movies are free and open to the public. \n\nSaturday\, June 13: The Parent Trap (1998; PG)\nSaturday\, June 27: Lilo & Stitch (2002; PG)\nFriday\, July 3: National Treasure (2004; PG)\nSaturday\, July 11: A Bug’s Life (1998; G) (weather reschedule from 6/20)\n\nBe sure to get to the Commons early to snag your spot on the lawn. Guests are welcome to bring blankets or lawn chairs to settle in for the movie. \n+++ \nTo inquire about sponsorship opportunities and ways to get involved\, email community@hermannpark.org.
URL:https://hermannpark.org/event/kicking-it-at-hermann-park/
LOCATION:The Commons
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://hermannpark.org/wp-content/uploads/2026/05/Kicking-it-at-the-Commons-Square.jpg
END:VEVENT
